{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZaiXsMzuX7Z3yncW899","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Requirement, restated**: Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that confirms shipments (transitions from CREATED to CONFIRMED), succeeds idempotently on already-CONFIRMED shipments, rejects CANCELLED shipments with 409, and returns 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings** (path:line):\n- Controller: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` - currently has POST create, GET by ID, and GET list\n- Data model: `Shipment.kt:9-14` and `ShipmentStatus` enum `Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- Repository: `InMemoryShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` - has save(), findById(), existsById()\n- Tests: `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23-84` - uses MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n- Error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` defines ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` defines ErrorCode enum (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- Global error handler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` wraps ApiExceptions in ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has**:\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions (never build error bodies directly)\n- ResourceNotFoundException for 404 with ErrorCode; ConflictException for 409 with ErrorCode\n- All errors wrapped in ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- ResponseEntity with explicit HttpStatus (e.g., HttpStatus.CREATED)\n- Tests use MockMvc.perform() with status() and jsonPath() assertions\n- Repository provides simple save/findById/existsById methods\n- Shipment is a data class with immutable fields\n\n**Affected files** (why each cannot be avoided):\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the confirm endpoint here\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests covering the four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED, CANCELLED→409, unknown→404)\n3. `ApiError.kt` - Must add a new error code for rejecting CANCELLED shipments (e.g., SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n\n**Risks**:\n- Adding a new error code could affect other parts of the codebase if they try to enumerate or validate codes\n- If the shipment is not properly persisted after confirmation, idempotent retries might show stale data\n- Creating a copy of the shipment with new status could be overlooked\n\n**Open questions**: None identified; the ticket is clear on all four cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file**:\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** (lines 31-37): Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** (after line 56): Add new endpoint:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   This endpoint will:\n   - Find shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, descriptive message)\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - Return the saved (or unchanged) shipment\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** (after line 84): Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` - POST to confirm endpoint, expect 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment` - confirm twice, expect 200 both times, state unchanged on second\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment` - set up CANCELLED shipment in repo, confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment` - confirm unknown ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected**:\n- Creating a service layer between controller and repository: This would add complexity beyond what is needed. The existing code keeps everything in the controller for simplicity. Adding a service would require changes to the OrderController too (to be consistent), which is out of scope and violates \"no unrelated production file changes.\"\n- Reusing an existing error code instead of adding SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE: The existing codes (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) don't semantically fit a state-based rejection. Adding a new code is cleaner and more maintainable.\n- Making confirm() return ResponseEntity with explicit status: The existing getById() returns Shipment directly and relies on GlobalExceptionHandler for errors. For consistency, confirm() should also return Shipment directly.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n\nFor `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n\n1. **CREATED shipment** (happy path):\n   - Input: shipmentId path parameter\n   - Find shipment in repository by ID\n   - Check status: if CREATED, create new Shipment instance with status=CONFIRMED\n   - Call repository.save() with the updated shipment\n   - Return the saved Shipment (200 OK with Shipment in body, implicit via GlobalExceptionHandler)\n\n2. **CONFIRMED shipment** (idempotent):\n   - Input: shipmentId path parameter\n   - Find shipment in repository by ID\n   - Check status: if CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (no save call needed, but returning it is still correct)\n   - Return the Shipment (200 OK)\n\n3. **CANCELLED shipment** (error case):\n   - Input: shipmentId path parameter\n   - Find shipment in repository by ID\n   - Check status: if CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, \"Cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\")\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 with ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Non-existent shipment** (error case):\n   - Input: shipmentId path parameter\n   - Try to find shipment in repository by ID\n   - findById() returns null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"No shipment with id '...'\")\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 404 with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy**:\n\n1. `confirmCreatedShipment` - Create shipment (status=CREATED), POST confirm, verify 200, verify status is now CONFIRMED\n2. `confirmConfirmedShipmentIsIdempotent` - Create shipment, POST confirm, POST confirm again, verify both succeed, verify status is CONFIRMED both times\n3. `confirmCancelledShipmentIsRejected` - Create shipment and manually set it to CANCELLED in repo (using direct save), POST confirm, verify 409, verify error code is SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n4. `confirmNonExistentShipmentIsRejected` - POST confirm to unknown ID, verify 404, verify error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3319,"cache_read_input_tokens":17856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3319},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2809348-b88e-43c2-b1cc-615f7d6775b0","uuid":"ae186362-5b73-40c3-8567-0703c765bc7b","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:57:10.351Z","request_id":"req_011CfZaiXSKNxnt7J8JjzquW"}
